<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bayan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1902</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Bayang, Battle of Pandapatan · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moro-rebellion">Moro Rebellion</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bayan, also called the Battle of Bayang or Pandapatan, was fought on 2 May 1902 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lanao">Lake Lanao</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> troops and Maranao warriors. American forces under Colonel Frank Baldwin stormed the Maranao fortifications at Bayang after Maranao attacks on US troops. It was the first major clash of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moro-rebellion">Moro Rebellion</a> and opened the American campaigns to bring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lanao">Lanao</a> region under control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bayan.jpg" alt="Battle of Bayan" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Engineer Battalion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Bayan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
